<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1,2</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install the 2 nuts.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C154929" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>240</t-value1>
<t-value2>2450</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Wipe off any dirt from the tightening surface of the shock absorber lower side.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install front brake flexible hose No.1 with the bolt.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C117404" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>29</t-value1>
<t-value2>296</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not twist the flexible hose and speed sensor when installing them.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install the speed sensor FR LH with the bolt and clamp.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C153575" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>29</t-value1>
<t-value2>296</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not twist the flexible hose and speed sensor when installing them.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install the front tire.</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>103</t-value1>
<t-value2>1050</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Lower the vehicle and bounce it up and down several times to stabilize the front suspension.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Inspect the camber again.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If fine adjustment of the camber is necessary after the camber inspection, move the lower side of the shock absorber and adjust using the play between the bolts and the bolt holes of the steering knuckle.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000VNQ00LX_01_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___00005PY00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Side Slip</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Inspect the side slip using a side slip tester.</ptxt>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0 ±5mm (per 1m)</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Drive onto the side slip tester in a straight line at walking speed (approximately 4km/h) or less, with the transmission in neutral.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not apply the brakes on the side slip tester.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not turn the steering wheel on the side slip tester.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>If the result is not as specified, inspect the wheel alignment.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000VNQ00LX_01_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___00005PZ00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Toe-in</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Bounce the vehicle to stabilize it.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Push the vehicle forward 5m in a straight line by hand.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>When the vehicle has been moved backward, always move it forward by the same distance.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Align the height of the toe-in gauge pointer with the height of the front wheel axle center, and place it behind the tires.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C148423J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Mark the tread center at the rear of each front tire, and measure the distance between the marks (dimension B).</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Slowly push the vehicle forward to rotate the front wheels 180°.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not rotate the wheels more than 180°. If they are over-rotated, start again from setting the toe-in gauge.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Measure the distance between the marks at the front of the vehicle (dimension A).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C148424J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Calculate the toe-in.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="1" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="4.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Toe-in [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2±2</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Toe-in = B measurement - A measurement</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000VNQ00LX_01_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___00005Q000000">
<ptxt>Adjust Toe-in</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C117424" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<s2>
<ptxt>Measure the lengths of the threaded portions of the left and right rack ends.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="1" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="4.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Left-Right Difference [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1.5 or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Left-right difference 1.5mm or less</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the rack boot clips.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Loosen the tie rod end lock nuts.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>If the left-right difference of the rack end threaded portions is not as specified, adjust it.</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>If the toe-in measurement is off toward the toe-out side, adjust by extending the rack end with the shorter dimension.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>If the toe-in measurement is off toward the toe-in side, adjust by shortening the rack end with the longer dimension.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Inspect the toe-in again.</ptxt>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Turn the left and right rack ends equal amounts in opposite directions to adjust the toe-in to within the specified range.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="1" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="4.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Toe-in [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2±2</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Tighten the tie rod end lock nuts.</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>74</t-value1>
<t-value2>755</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Hold the hexagonal portion of the steering rack end so that the lock nut and steering rack end do not turn together, temporarily tighten the lock nut, and then tighten it while holding the width across flats of the tie rod end.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using pliers, install the clips to the steering rack boots.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not twist the boots when installing them.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000VNQ00LX_01_0006" proc-id="RM0550J___00005Q100000">
<ptxt>Inspect Wheel Angle</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C148075J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<s2>
<ptxt>Set the turning radius gauge.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Inspect the wheel angle.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title/>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.39in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Drive Type</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inside (inspection range)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Outside (reference)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>FF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>39°17'±2'</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>33°04'</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4WD</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>38°41'±2'</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>32°52'</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Perform with the vehicle unladen (without spare tire and tools).</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>With the vehicle unladen, inspect with the foot brake applied using a brake pedal depressor or equivalent so that the front wheels do not rotate.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Remove the stop light fuse before inspecting so that the stop lights do not illuminate.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000VNQ00LX_01_0012">
<ptxt>Check Front Wheels Straight-ahead Position</ptxt>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000VNQ00LX_01_0013" proc-id="RM0550J___0000BU900000">
<ptxt>Disconnect Battery Negative Terminal</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>Disconnect the battery negative terminal for 2 seconds or more.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000VNQ00LX_01_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___0000BUA00000">
<ptxt>Connect Battery Negative Terminal</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>5.4</t-value1>
<t-value2>55</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</content1>
</s-1>
